-	\textbf{Model Parameter}: The SE-GNN backbone uses three stacked GATv2 layers (64 hidden dimensions, four heads) with LayerNorm and LeakyReLU ($\alpha = 0.2$). Nodes carry four semantic features (acceptance, SCC membership, initialization, distance to acceptance) and edges carry six features (one-hot edge type plus semantic distances); global attention pooling (Eq.~\ref{eq:readout}) summarizes structure. Short- and long-term value networks are two-layer MLPs (256 and 128 hidden units, respectively) producing scalar estimates, while the fusion gate $\beta(q)$ is computed by a lightweight 64-hidden-unit MLP, echoing hypernetwork-style conditioning~\citep{klocek2019hypernetwork}. We set $\gamma = 3$ and $\theta = 0.5$ to place the fusion midpoint at medium proximity, tuned on $\varphi_2$. Training uses PPO for 1{,}000{,}000 timesteps (batch 64, learning rate $3 \times 10^{-4}$, Adam), RL discount $\gamma_{\text{RL}} = 0.998$, clipped advantages $[-1,1]$, and evaluation results are reported as the mean over seeds 1--5, with 500 episodes per seed. The baseline configuration reproduces DeepLTL~\citep{deepltl}, and each ablation toggles HV, MSGNN, and tracking relative to this reference.
